fact WorkItem(id: "WI-998", description: some(value: "Implements 059 R4 clauses 1 and 2 — FILL, never DISPLACE — on top of the pass-1\ndeclaration ledger. Spec: docs/proposals/059-secondary-entries.md.\n\nCLAUSE 1 — TWO SUPPLIERS OF ONE MEMBER NAME ARE REFUSED AT LOAD, naming both sites.\n058 §3.1's coexistence-gated-on-nameability: two providers of a SPEC may coexist\nbecause an ambiguous call has a repair the author can write (`[Spec = W]`); two\nmembers of one sort under one name have no such currency — `r.peek()` cannot say\nwhich — so this is the case 058 calls \"coexistence one cannot select out of is a\ntrap, not a feature\". Applies to two secondary entries, and to two same-named\noperations in one main entry.\n\nCLAUSE 2 — A SECONDARY ENTRY MAY NOT REDECLARE A MEMBER THE MAIN ENTRY DECLARES AND\nIMPLEMENTS. 058 §3.6's no-displacement, in its own words: fill silence, never\noverwrite speech.\n\n\"IMPLEMENTS\" IS NOT \"HAS A BODY\", AND GETTING THIS WRONG SILENTLY DISCARDS THE FILL.\nMEASURED: `sort String`'s `isEmpty` is declared body-less in stdlib and mapped to\n`string_is_empty` by an `operation_map` in anthill-stl. A secondary entry supplying\n`operation isEmpty(s: String) -> Bool = false` — wrong for every input — LOADS CLEAN\nAND NEVER RUNS: `\"\".isEmpty()` still answers true and `\"x\".isEmpty()` still false,\nidentical to the control with no secondary entry at all. The author is told nothing.\nThe mechanism: `call_op_sym` and `call_op_bridged` BOTH return a registered builtin\nbefore any body lookup, and an `operation_map` clause arrives there AS a registered\nbuiltin (`register_operation_mappings` -> `register_builtin_sym`).\n\nSO SILENCE MEANS NO IMPLEMENTATION FROM ANY SOURCE — no anthill body, no\n`operation_map`/`const_map` entry for the target language, no registered builtin —\nand a fill over a declaration backed by any of them is REFUSED, naming the backing.\n\nNOT A CORNER CASE: counting `operation_map` entries in anthill-stl, Float has 29,\nString 13, Int64 9, BigInt 7, persistence 6 = 64 members that read as \"silence\" under\na body-only test.\n\n`[simp]` IS A FOURTH CASE AND A DIFFERENT ONE — name it, do not fold it in. A `[simp]`\nequation does not BACK the operation (WI-818/885), but the typer rewrites LHS->RHS\nbefore dispatch, so a filled body is dead at every rewritten call site and live\neverywhere else.\n\nWHERE THE CHECK RUNS. Clause 1 is a pure ledger walk in pass 1. Clause 2 SPLITS: the\nledger decides \"redeclared\", but \"already implemented\" can only be read after the\n`anthill.realization.OperationMapping` facts exist — and the declaration and its\nmapping routinely live in different crates (String's declaration in stdlib, its\nmapping in anthill-stl). So clause 2 needs a post-pass-2 read as well.\n\nWHAT THIS CLAUSE IS FOR, and why the body-less carve-out must survive: it carries\nSPEC-AUTHOR AND IMPLEMENTER AS DIFFERENT HANDS — one writes the sort and its\nsignatures, another (often an AI agent) supplies the bodies in anthill, and the\ninterface it must meet is checkable rather than conventional. The signature stays the\nmain entry's and the filling entry may not change it.\n\nMEASURED BLAST RADIUS: 0 sites for both clauses. Honest but easy — the corpus\ncontains no secondary entries at all, so clause 2 has nothing to bite on yet.\nCONTROL: a fill over a body-less-AND-unimplemented member must still LOAD (that is the\ncapability); a fill over `String.isEmpty` must newly FAIL, and today passes."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-997", "WI-1003"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Rejected(reason: "Superseded by WI-1049 and the 2026-08-08 proposal 059 decision. WI-1049 already refuses every second operation declaration; proposal 059 now refuses bodyless operations in secondary entries instead of allowing another declaration to fill them. Implementation belongs to WI-1000.", at: "2026-08-08T13:21:17Z"))
